From e9633dea96093e85a2b34e8d98d4b071acfef664 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 15:10:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Phase 1b hardening: SSRF pinning, rate limits, roles,
 worker token, CI

- Outbound fetches to user-supplied URLs (site scanner, contact
  enrichment) go through src/lib/net/public-network.ts: the private
  address check runs inside undici's connect-time DNS lookup, closing the
  DNS-rebinding window; blocklist now covers CGNAT, IPv4-mapped,
  compatible, NAT64 and 6to4 IPv6, and non-web ports
- DB-backed rate limiting shared across instances (login per IP and per
  account, review feedback, report view/CTA counting), via the existing
  atomic studio_take_limit(); in-memory fallback if the DB is down
- Role checks for settings and provider-credential changes; settings
  PATCH uses an allow-list schema (no mass assignment)
- Review feedback requires an existing, active campaign
- Scoped AGENT_WORKER_TOKEN for the local agent (six endpoints only);
  worker and installer support it, passcode remains a fallback; bearer
  API calls with bad tokens get a 401 instead of a login page
- Fix: the follow-up scheduler endpoint was blocked by the login gate,
  so scheduled follow-ups were never sent
- Constant-time comparison for the automation secret; HSTS header
- GitHub Actions CI: typecheck, unit tests, build, SQL security tests,
  gitleaks
- 83 unit tests (58 new)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
